    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the number of different orders in which Jordan's relay team can run, given that Jordan is running the fourth lap, we need to calculate the number of permutations of the remaining three team members (assuming Jordan is the fourth runner).\n\nThe number of permutations \\(P(n, n)\\) where \\(n\\) is the total number of items to arrange is simply \\(n!\\) (n factorial), which is the product of all positive integers up to \\(n\\).\n\nHere, we have 4 team members, and we want to find the number of ways to arrange these 4 members. The calculation is as follows:\n\n\\[ P(4, 4) = 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 24 \\]\n\nLet's verify this calculation using Python.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Number of team members\nn = 4\n\n# Calculate the number of permutations of 4 items\nnum_permutations = math.factorial(n)\nprint(num_permutations)\n```\n```output\n24\n```\nThe number of different orders in which Jordan's relay team can run, assuming that Jordan runs the fourth lap, is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).",
